{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>His wife.</b> On account of his wife, like \"lest they say to me\" (Judges 9:54)." "For ירא is a past-tense verb, and likewise \"And it came to pass, when Isaac was old\" (Genesis 27:1), and the words \"for he said, lest they kill me\" are missing, and likewise \"for Elohim has made me fruitful\" (Genesis 41:52)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The lemma 'his wife' in the verse is understood by Ibn Ezra as 'on account of his wife,' glossed by the parallel in Judges 9:54."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:53.629986239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}